## Browser and context discipline

Your context is metered after every tool call and you are force-stopped at {{HARD_PCT}}% of the window; every token
spent on a page dump is a test not run.
- One `take_snapshot` per page state, then act by uid. Do not re-snapshot to "check" a page you just read.
- For a specific value use `evaluate_script` returning a short string (an element's innerText, sliced), not a snapshot.
- `take_screenshot` ALWAYS with `filePath` (`{{RUN}}/evidence/{ID}/{step}.png`) so the image is saved, not returned.
  Look at a screenshot only when layout is the thing under test.
- `list_network_requests` / `list_console_messages`: always filter and page them.
- Read one test file at a time; grep logs; never print whole files you only need a line from.

## When a step needs {{OWNER}}: pause ONLY for {{PAUSE_FOR}}

- **Pause** only for {{PAUSE_FOR}}. Get everything around it ready, then
  `{{PYTHON}} ledger.py pause {ID} "the ask" --signin`, write HANDOFF.md and end your reply. The ask is self-contained:
  which window (the run's Chrome: tabs on {{APP_URL}}, profile `{{RUN}}/chrome-profile`), the URL to start from,
  exactly what to do and what to pick, what to leave open, and what you will check after.
- **Everything else** that needs a person or something this stack cannot do alone: do every part you can, record what you
  checked with `ledger.py note`, then `{{PYTHON}} ledger.py needs {ID} "the exact ask"` (recorded as blocked; the ask goes
  on the run's live page for {{OWNER}} to answer) and go straight on to the next test. Never pause for these, never
  guess, never work around them.
- {{OWNER}} follows the run on its live page, which shows each test's result line and every ask as you write them. Write
  them in plain words: what the person using the app saw, and where. Keep selectors and file names for notes.

## Context guard and hand-off

You will get `[context guard]` messages after tool calls. On the first one: start nothing new, finish only the step in
flight, record it in the ledger, write HANDOFF.md, end your reply. At {{HARD_PCT}}% the session is ended for you mid-step;
the next session recovers from the ledger, so keep the ledger current at all times.

HANDOFF.md (≤ 40 lines, only what the ledger does not already hold):
- In-flight test and the exact next step (or "none, {ID} recorded").
- Records created but not yet in the ledger (ids, reference numbers, test-data names).
- Browser state: tabs open, signed in where, anything mid-dialog.
- Environment lessons from this session the next one needs (a route that works, a quirk, a slow page).

